{"text": "PRIVILEGED & CONFIDENTIAL -- ATTORNEY NOTES TO FILE\nHollis, Marchetti & Thibodeaux, P.C.                         File No. EP-2026-0388\n\nESTATE PLANNING CONFERENCE -- dictated by Winifred Hollis (WH), typed dhp\n\nClient:      CASTELLANOS-BRANDT, EVELYN R.  (goes by \"Evie\")\nDOB:         April 2, 1935  (age 91)\nSSN:         336 56 2821\nHome:        88 Larkspur Lane, Wauwatosa, WI 53213\nPhone:       414 555 0106 (landline only; she does not carry a cell)\nConference:  Thursday, September 17, 2026, at the client's home, 1:30 to 3:45 pm\n\nAlso present: her daughter Marisol Brandt-Okafor (by video from Tucson) for the first half hour;\ncaregiver Bernadette \"Bernie\" Kowalczyk, who let me in and then left the room at my request.\nDong-hyun Park from our office attended to take the asset list and act as second observer.\n\n1. CAPACITY AND HEALTH\n\nMrs. Castellanos-Brandt was alert, funny, and entirely clear about who her family is and what she\nowns. She corrected me twice on dates. Her primary care doctor, Dr. Farrukh Siddiqui of\nWauwatosa Senior Health Partners, saw her on Aug. 28, 2026 and scored her 27/30 on the MoCA; his letter\nis in the file. No diagnosis of dementia. She does have macular degeneration (we will print\neverything in 16-point type), wears hearing aids, and has atrial fibrillation for which she takes\napixaban 2.5 mg twice daily. A pacemaker was implanted in 2021. She told me she wants\nno feeding tube and no \"machines\" if there is no reasonable hope of recovery.\nI am satisfied she meets the standard in Wis. Stat. § 853.03, and I saw no sign that anyone\nwas steering her. Marisol spoke only when asked.\n\n2. FAMILY\n\nFirst husband Rafael Castellanos, died 11/04/1978. Second husband Dieter Brandt, died\nFebruary 9, 2019. No surviving spouse. Children and descendants:\n\n  (a) Rafael Castellanos Jr. (\"Rafe\"), born in the summer of 1959, single, no children.\n      Lives rent-free in the client's lake cabin (see below).\n  (b) Marisol Brandt-Okafor, born 7/22/1964, married, two adult children, lives at\n      6140 E. Calle Ojos Verdes, Tucson, AZ 85750. Cell (520) 555-0171;\n      marisol.bo@desertmail.example.\n  (c) Annelise Brandt, who died of ovarian cancer in 2011. Annelise is survived by one son,\n      Jonah Brandt-Whitehorse, now 24. Jonah has autism spectrum disorder and receives SSI.\n      He lives in a group home run by Prairie Oak Supported Living, Inc. in Waukesha. His father\n      is an enrolled member of the Ho-Chunk Nation and is not involved.\n\nStepson: Klaus Brandt, Dieter's son from his first marriage, a German citizen living in Stuttgart.\nEvie is fond of Klaus but says \"he has plenty.\"\n\n3. THE PROBLEM WITH RAFE (client asked that this stay out of any letter mailed to the cabin)\n\nRafe has two OWI convictions, the last in 2019, and completed inpatient alcohol treatment in 2020.\nEvie believes he is drinking again. He filed Chapter 7 in 2016 (Bankr. E.D. Wis.,\nNo. 16-24817-gmh). Since then she has lent him money \"whenever he asked\" -- she\nthinks about thirty-eight thousand five hundred dollars, none of it documented; her check\nregister supports roughly $36,900. She does not want him cut out. She wants his share\nheld in trust with someone other than family deciding distributions. He does not know\nshe is meeting with a lawyer, and she asked that we not call him. (His number, for the\nfile only: 920-555-0139.)\n\n4. ASSETS (from her handwritten list and the statements Marisol scanned)\n\n  Residence, 88 Larkspur Lane. Assessed at $412,000. No mortgage. Titled in her name alone.\n  Lake cabin, N7714 Loon Hollow Road, Elkhart Lake, WI 53020 (Sheboygan County). She\n    guesses 365k. In the family since 1966. Property tax parcel 59016-204471.\n  Pontoon boat kept at the cabin, the \"Second Wind\", registration WS 4471 KC.\n  2020 Buick Enclave, VIN 5GAEVAKW7LX662444, plate ALK-2291. She stopped driving in March;\n    Bernie drives it for errands.\n  Lakeshore Community Credit Union (\"LCCU\"), routing 064705723:\n    checking 0071-4436612, balance $23,418.77; savings ending -8840, balance $61,050.\n    Safe deposit box #214 at the Mayfair branch. The key is in the blue teapot.\n  Halvorsen Whitlock Securities, brokerage account HW-338-221904, about $1.14 million. This\n    account was retitled JOINT with Marisol in 2022 \"so she could help pay bills.\"\n  IRA at Halvorsen Whitlock, account 7Q4-118835, about $286,000. The beneficiary on file is\n    still Dieter.\n  Midwest Fraternal Life policy MFL-0092-55431, face amount $50,000; beneficiary is\n    St. Hedwig's Catholic Parish.\n  Dieter's watch collection, appraised in 2019 at $27,300.\n  Digital: e-mail evie.cb1935@mailbox.example, password written on an index card taped inside\n    the desk drawer (Dieter1961!). iPad, serial DMPXK2Q7HG5F; passcode 0402.\n\n  Rough total $2.25 million, well under the federal exemption. No Form 709 has ever been filed.\n\n5. WHAT SHE WANTS\n\n  Specific gifts: $25,000 to St. Hedwig's (she is a lifelong Catholic and still tithes); $10,000 to\n  Menomonee Valley Animal Rescue; $5,000 to Bernie \"if she is still with me\"; the watch\n  collection to Klaus. She mentioned she is a longtime donor to the county Democratic Party but\n  wants nothing political in the will.\n\n  Residue in three equal shares: one to Marisol outright; one for Rafe in a discretionary\n  trust; one for Jonah in a supplemental needs trust drafted so that he keeps SSI and\n  Medicaid. Trustee of both trusts: Great Lakes Fiduciary Trust Co., with Marisol holding the\n  power to remove and replace.\n\n  The cabin: Rafe may stay up to five years if he pays the taxes and insurance; then it is\n  sold and the proceeds fall into the residue. The boat goes with the cabin.\n\n  Health care agent: Marisol. Alternate: her niece Dr. Guadalupe Castellanos (\"Lupe\"),\n  the only hospice physician in Door County. Financial agent: Marisol; alternate: the trust company.\n\n  She also wants a HIPAA release naming Marisol and Lupe, so that the doctors will actually talk\n  to them. Last winter, when Evie was admitted for pneumonia at Kinnickinnic Valley Hospital for six days\n  (in on Jan 9, home on the 15th), nobody there would tell Marisol anything for the first two\n  days, and \"Evelyn was not about to let that happen twice,\" as she put it.\n\n  Burial beside Dieter at Holy Cross Cemetery, Section 14, lot 203-B. Funeral Mass at St. Hedwig's.\n\n6. ISSUES I RAISED\n\n  - The joint brokerage account defeats the three-way split: at death it passes to Marisol\n    alone. Marisol volunteered, before I said anything, that it should be undone. Plan:\n    create the Castellanos-Brandt Revocable Trust and retitle the account to it. Call the adviser,\n    Thaddeus Nwosu (\"Tad\"), direct 414.555.0155, tad.nwosu@hwsecurities.example.\n  - IRA beneficiary form must be redone now; do not wait for signing.\n  - Gift to a paid caregiver. Bernie is employed through Comfort Hearth Home Care LLC at\n    $31 an hour. Check the agency's policy on gifts. I will see Evie alone again before signing and\n    document that the gift is her own idea. Kowalczyk has worked for her since January 2023.\n  - Loans to Rafe: treat as advancements, or forgive? She wants them forgiven. Put it in writing.\n  - She and Dieter signed a marital property agreement on June 30, 1994. Neither she nor\n    Marisol can find it. Ask Prairie Oak nothing about this; ask the credit union to list the\n    contents of the box.\n  - Jonah: confirm with his case manager that a third-party trust will not count as his resource.\n\n7. FEES AND NEXT STEPS\n\n  Quoted a flat fee of $4,800 for the trust, pour-over will, two powers of attorney, and\n  the supplemental needs trust. Retainer of $1,500 received, her check no. 3318.\n  Drafts to client (large print) and to Marisol by 10/02/2026. Signing at the house on\n  Tuesday the 13th of October at 10:30; Park and I will witness. Dr. Siddiqui's office will\n  fax an updated capacity note the week before: fax (414) 555-0190.\n\nWH/dhp", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "1,258 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Hollis", "Marchetti", "Thibodeaux", "Winifred Hollis", "Evelyn R. Castellanos-Brandt", "Marisol Brandt-Okafor", "Bernadette Kowalczyk", "Dong-hyun Park", "Rafael Castellanos", "Dieter Brandt", "Dr. Farrukh Siddiqui", "Rafael Castellanos Jr.", "Annelise Brandt", "Jonah Brandt-Whitehorse", "Klaus Brandt", "Evie", "Bernie", "St. Hedwig's Catholic Parish", "Marisol", "Rafe", "Jonah", "Klaus", "Dieter", "Vinnie", "Guadalupe Castellanos", "Lupe", "Kowalczyk", "Thaddeus Nwosu", "Tad", "Park", "Dr. Siddiqui"], "companies": ["Hollis, Marchetti & Thibodeaux, P.C.", "Wauwatosa Senior Health Partners", "Prairie Oak Supported Living, Inc.", "Lakeshore Community Credit Union", "Halvorsen Whitlock Securities", "Midwest Fraternal Life", "Great Lakes Fiduciary Trust Co", "Comfort Hearth Home Care LLC", "Holy Cross Cemetery", "Prairie Oak", "hwsecurities", "Kinnickinnic Valley Hospital", "Trust company", "St. Hedwig's", "credit union", "Peace Hearth Home Care LLC", "Evelyn", "WH", "dhp"]}, "chunks": 5, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.19999999925494194, "modelMs": 73562.70000000112, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "passport_dl", "routing", "phone", "record", "vin", "account", "money", "dob", "age90", "date", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 52, "end": 88, "text": "Hollis, Marchetti & Thibodeaux, P.C.", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Hollis, Marchetti & Thibodeaux, P.C."}, {"start": 122, "end": 134, "text": "EP-2026-0388", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "EP-2026-0388"}, {"start": 178, "end": 193, "text": "Winifred Hollis", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Winifred Hollis"}, {"start": 195, "end": 197, "text": "WH", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canon